			"notes": "### Vehicles, Customization & Loot\n* **4 Cart Tiers & Unique Models:** Added Standard, Swift, Sturdy, and Prime — each featuring **brand-new custom 3D models**, unique stats, and uncraftable tier cores found as rare loot in structure chests.\n* **In-World Customization:** Replaced 16 separate colored cart items with dynamic in-world dyeing (all 16 dyes) and sponge paint stripping.\n* **Survival Economy:** Standardized fuel strictly to pure Coal (+15 FU) and repairs to Iron Ingots (+15 HP), both with anti-waste protection.\n\n### Physics, Driving & Collisions\n* **Smooth Movement & Dynamics:** Overhauled movement physics for butter-smooth driving, natural slope climbing, and realistic airborne momentum and knockback impulses.\n* **Transmission & Braking:** Added reverse gear with tier-based speeds, smooth shifting transitions, and dedicated braking with dynamic squeal audio.\n* **Complete Collision Overhaul:** Added brand-new cart-to-cart (C2C) collisions, universal crash consequences (safe bumps vs high-speed crashes with fuel leaks and stun), and expanded entity interactions (mobs, primed TNT, crystals, armor stands).\n* **Environmental Hazards:** Added foliage drag through leaves, shallow water resistance, deep water engine flooding/sinking, and fire/lava damage.\n\n### Visuals, Audio & Polish\n* **Audio & Animations:** Overhauled sound logic with tier-specific engine hums, shift clicks, and water sputters; added client-synced steering animations, reverse steering fixes, and improved particle effects.\n* **HUD & Optimization:** Enhanced the in-ride dashboard to blend with tiered stats, optimized overall mod performance, and smoothed out multiplayer/Replay mod syncing.\n* **Branding & Documentation:** Renamed mod display name to **Terracarts**, updated `fabric.mod.json`, refreshed `LICENSE.md`, and completely rewrote `README.md`."
		},
